Note: Aggregating records into a Dict: counts and totals per key.
Note: Dicts are persistent: set returns a new dict, so we fold with reduce.
use "@core"

Note: The raw log is one comma-separated string.
Strings orders = (split "tea,coffee,tea,cocoa,coffee,tea" ",")
Ints prices = (list 3 4 3 5 4 3)

Note: Count occurrences; insertion order is first-seen order.
Dict<String, Int> counts = (reduce orders (dict) (fn Dict<String, Int> acc, String item => (set acc item (add (getOr acc item 0) 1))))

(each counts (fn String item, Int n => (print $"{item}: {n}")))

Note: Revenue per item from parallel arrays.
Dict<String, Int> revenue = (reduce (zip orders prices) (dict) (fn Dict<String, Int> acc, Void pair => (set acc pair@0 (add (getOr acc pair@0 0) pair@1))))
(print $"revenue items: {(str (keys revenue))}")
(print $"revenue values: {(str (values revenue))}")

Note: Keep only items ordered more than once.
Dict<String, Int> popular = (filter counts (fn String item, Int n => (gt n 1)))
(print $"popular: {(str (keys popular))}")
(print $"distinct items: {(size counts)}")
